   "id": "root",
   "x": 70,
   "y": 10,
   "w": 760,
   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "Acutely confused older adult: DELIRIUM? Then FIND THE TRIGGER",
   "lines": [
    "delirium = an ACUTE, FLUCTUATING change in attention and awareness",
    "the QUIET one is missed: HYPOACTIVE (drowsy, lethargic) is the commonest, mistaken for DEPRESSION",
    "screen with the 4-AT: < 2 minutes, no special training"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_4",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 156,
   "w": 810,
   "h": 78,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "4-AT ≥ 4: POSSIBLE DELIRIUM → hunt EVERY trigger (DIMES + 3 Ps)",
   "lines": [
    "• clearly abnormal ALERTNESS, or an ACUTE change / fluctuation: 4 points EACH",
    "• 1–3: possible cognitive impairment (COGNITIVE DECLINE chart) · 0: neither"
   ]
  },
